# Project Workflow (项目运行工作流)

When working on **planning**, **execution**, or **documentation** for this project, follow this rule and consult **docs/index.md** for the document index.

## Core document triangle

- **docs/REQUIREMENTS.md** — product requirements (R-M*, R-C*, R-H*, R-B*, R-A*, R-DV*).
- **docs/ARCHITECTURE.md** — system architecture and run environment (§2).
- **docs/plans/CAPABILITY_TRACKING.md** — capability dimensions, current progress and gaps.

Modify these documents **only** when the **user (or project owner) explicitly** requests a change in **product requirements**, **hardware / run environment / architecture**, or **capability assessment**. After such a change, keep the three documents consistent.

## Supporting resources (read-only reference)

- **docs/DATABASE.md** — PostgreSQL schema and write strategies.
- **docs/research/*** and **docs/fsm/*** — state space, FSM, Guard tuning, config safety taxonomy.

## Decision flow

Whether to adjust requirements, architecture, or capability assessment is decided by the **project owner**. The agent follows the owner's instruction and updates the relevant core document(s).
